## XXIV. The "Assume Nothing Useful Was Done" Protocol (2026-06-13)

1. **Mandatory Post-Development Heuristic Auditing**:
   - In accordance with the "Assume Nothing Useful Was Done" protocol, you must never trust your own generation or minor tests to prove success. Assume your edits have introduced regressions, key leaks, or type comparison errors on untested dates.
   - You must run the 365-day automated heuristic audit via pytest (`pytest tests/test_all_days_compliance.py`) to verify that all 365 days of the calendar year are free from formatting failures, leaked programmer keys, and runtime crashes.
   - Any model failing to verify 100% daily coverage across the entire annual cycle is in direct violation of project compliance rules.

2. **Jumbled Commemoration Separation Gate**:
   - Every day in the calendar database ([calendar_dolnytsky.json](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/json_db/calendar_dolnytsky.json)) that contains multiple independent commemorations must have them split into separate dictionaries inside the `entries` array.
   - Semicolons `;` in raw text descriptions must always be split into individual elements. Jumbling them as a single string is strictly prohibited.

